🔑 Key principle (important)
Validation data does not improve the model.
Training data does.

So if your goal is “keep as much useful data as possible”, you want:

as much data as possible in training

only enough data in validation to be statistically stable

Moving data from train → val:

❌ does not improve generalization

❌ does not reduce file size meaningfully

