Ah — this error is different and actually very informative 👍

SyntaxError: Unexpected end of JSON input

This almost always means:

👉 Your .ipynb file on GitHub is corrupted or incomplete.

Colab is trying to read the notebook (which is just a JSON file internally), but the JSON is broken.

🔎 Why this happens
Most common causes:

1️⃣ The notebook upload was interrupted
The file did not fully upload to GitHub.

2️⃣ The notebook was created manually
If you created the .ipynb file directly on GitHub using:

Add file → Create new file → part1.ipynb
without valid notebook JSON content, it will be invalid.

3️⃣ File is empty or partially saved
If you check the GitHub page and it looks like raw JSON instead of a rendered notebook preview, that’s a sign.

✅ How to fix it (correct way)
🥇 Recommended fix
Open the notebook in Google Colab

Make sure it runs

Click:

File → Download → Download .ipynb
Delete the broken notebook on GitHub

Upload the freshly downloaded .ipynb

That guarantees valid JSON.

🥈 Quick sanity check
Open this in your browser:

https://github.com/nairods/Scies4Free-FastML-tutorial/blob/main/part1.ipynb
If GitHub:

❌ Shows raw JSON text → broken file

❌ Says “Unable to render” → broken file

✅ Shows formatted notebook preview → file is valid

🧠 Why this happens technically
An .ipynb file is just structured JSON like:

{
 "cells": [...],
 "metadata": {...},
 "nbformat": 4,
 "nbformat_minor": 2
}
If the file ends halfway (e.g. missing closing }),
Colab throws:

Unexpected end of JSON input

🏁 Almost certainly your situation
You probably:

Created part1.ipynb directly in GitHub

Or renamed a .py file to .ipynb

Or upload was incomplete

