Your error:

ValueError: Cannot load file containing pickled data when allow_pickle=False
happens because np.load() defaults to allow_pickle=False in recent NumPy versions.

Your .npz file contains pickled arrays (this happens with structured arrays or anything saved via np.savez_compressed that isn’t plain numeric arrays).

