fit: computes the mean and standard deviation from the training data only.

transform: applies the standardization to the training data.

transform(X_test)

Uses the same mean and standard deviation from the training set to scale the test set.

Ensures that the test data is on the same scale as the training data, without “leaking” info from the test set.

Why it’s important
Many ML algorithms (especially neural networks, SVMs, and distance-based methods) perform better when all features are on the same scale.

Without scaling, features with large numeric ranges can dominate the learning process.

Scaling only on the training set avoids data leakage, which is crucial for a fair evaluation.

