Adding a Google Colab link to your GitHub notebook is simple and a common practice in tutorials. There are a few ways to do it depending on where you want the link to appear. Here’s a clean approach:

1. Use a Badge at the Top of Your Notebook
You can add a Markdown cell at the very top of your notebook with a clickable Colab badge. For example:

[![Open In Colab](https://colab.research.google.com/assets/colab-badge.svg)](https://colab.research.google.com/github/YOUR_USERNAME/YOUR_REPO/blob/main/YOUR_NOTEBOOK.ipynb)
Replace YOUR_USERNAME with your GitHub username.

Replace YOUR_REPO with your repository name.

