That means the network outputs something like:

[0.02, 0.80, 0.05, 0.10, 0.03]
This is a probability distribution over 5 classes.

Now the loss function must compare:

The predicted probability vector

The true label

How that comparison is done determines whether you need one-hot encoding.

🔹 Case 1 — Using categorical_crossentropy
This loss expects:

y_true = [0, 1, 0, 0, 0]
So if the correct class is class 1:

y_true = [0, 1, 0, 0, 0]
y_pred = [0.02, 0.80, 0.05, 0.10, 0.03]
