🔹 Case 2 — Using sparse_categorical_crossentropy
Here the true label is just:

y_true = 1
TensorFlow internally converts that into the equivalent one-hot form during loss computation.

So you can keep:

[0, 1, 4, 3, 2, ...]
No manual one-hot needed.

🔥 So Why Does One-Hot Exist?
Because mathematically, cross-entropy is defined between two probability distributions.

The one-hot vector represents:

"100% probability on the correct class"

🧠 Conceptual Interpretation
One-hot encoding turns:

“This jet is a W boson”

into:

“Probability distribution where P(W)=1 and others=0”

That matches the softmax output structure.

